# Frontend standards

- Use functional React components.
- Prefer feature-level code in `src/features/<FeatureName>/...` and shared/reusable code in `src/shared/...`.
- UI primitives/components shared across the app belong in `src/components/ui/...`.
- Use `wouter` routes inside `src/App.tsx` (via `Route`/`Switch`).
- Prefer Chakra UI components for layout/forms to match existing patterns.
- **Animation** ([Chakra UI — Animation](https://chakra-ui.com/docs/components/concepts/animation)):
  - Prefer **CSS animations** (keyframes + Chakra style props) for Chakra components — avoid heavy JS-driven animation libraries unless a use case truly needs them.
  - Disclosure components (dialog, popover, etc.) expose `data-state`: use **`_open`** when open and **`_closed`** when closed to style enter/exit.
  - Define **`@keyframes`** (e.g. fade-in / fade-out) and reference them via `animation` or `animationName` / `animationDuration` on those pseudo props.
  - **Compose** multiple animations with `animationName: "fade-in, scale-in"` (comma-separated) and set shared timing with `animationDuration` (and related longhands as needed).
- Keep imports clean:
  - Use `@/` aliases (from `src/*`).
  - Avoid long chains of relative imports.
